From e53da83f24ee66e22ca65b9bdd8e123fc002d716 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 05:19:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ga2: VU1 programs keyed by entry point and reachable code

Games upload VU1 microprograms in changing combinations, so whole-image
program keys kept missing in new scenes (Mugen tutorial battle, Zettai
ship map) and those scenes fell back to the interpreter. ga2_vu1_gen now
also emits one program per entry point, keyed by the entry pair and the
contents of the pairs reachable from it (ps2_vu1_reach.h), analysed from
those pairs alone. The runtime merges the programs that match an image into
a per-image chunk table; a pc no program covers (a run entry, a JR target)
is tried once as an entry, and GA2_VU1_DUMP records misses in
<hash>.entries for the next vu1gen. Chunks are only entered with nothing
pending. GA2_VU1JIT=entries checks entry programs alone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
